---
#1807: `t.core` declares `Repo`; `t.model` uses it in a record and a fn
signature; `t.web`, `t.page` and `t.vault` reach `Repo` only through those
declarations. `uses` is one level for naming, so none of them may write
`Repo`, but each imported declaration is resolved in its own scope: a
literal for `Run.repo` is checked and branded as a `Repo`, `r.repo` is typed
`Repo`, and `first(r)` returns one. They were typed by nothing before, so a
wrong value in any of these positions compiled.
---
commons t.core

type Repo = String where NonEmpty

fn Repo.shout(self) -> String {
  "\(self)!"
}

type Status = enum { Pending, Done }
